  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed rear extension would facilitate an outdoor seating area with a retractable roof and openable windows. Customer activity, including conversation and gatherings, is inherently unpredictable, and the Noise Impact Assessment submitted relates only to the kitchen extraction system, providing no assessment of noise from the outdoor seating area. In the absence of robust mitigation measures, the proposal is likely to significantly harm the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to and Chapter 15 of the NPPF (2024), Policies D13 and D14 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DMD 33, DMD 34 and DMD 68 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The extension is sited at the rear of the building and it has not been demonstrated that delivery and servicing operations could continue safely and effectively without obstruction from the structure. While the site benefits from a PTAL 4 location and the loss of six parking spaces is of lesser significance, the design and siting of the extension could compromise the operational functioning of the site. The proposal is therefore contrary to Chapter 9 of the NPPF (2024) and Policy T7 of London Plan (2021) requiring development to provide safe, efficient, and functional servicing arrangements.",
    "The proposed introduction of a new front entrance would disrupt the established hierarchy, rhythm and compositional order of the existing elevation, which currently relates positively to the neighbouring block and contributes to a coherent streetscape. The proposed entrance is out of keeping with the character and context of the host building and fails to respect its architectural composition. In addition, insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate how the significant change in level at the proposed entrance would be satisfactorily addressed, resulting in a poorly resolved and non-inclusive design. The proposal is therefore considered to represent poor design quality that would harm the character and appearance of the building and the street scene, contrary to Chapter 12 of the NPPF (2024), Policies D3 and D7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DMD 37, DMD 38, DMD 39 and DMD 40 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
